# Line endings are a property of this project, not of whoever cloned it.
#
# Without this, correctness depends on each contributor's global core.autocrlf.
# That matters more here than in most repos: yolodeck is a fork of a macOS project
# (agentsd) and the README tells you to `git diff upstream/main` to see what changed.
# Line-ending drift turns that diff into thousands of phantom changed lines and makes
# the comparison useless. Upstream's CI also runs on Linux, macOS, and Windows.
#
# text=auto  — normalize to LF in the repository, always
# eol=lf     — and check out as LF everywhere, including Windows
#
# All current tooling here (VS Code, PowerShell 7, Node, Git Bash) reads LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched. Git's heuristics usually get this right; being
# explicit means a corrupted plugin icon can't be one bad autodetect away.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.streamDeckPlugin binary
*.streamDeckProfile binary
